text:
@Einzelgänger, I appreciate the thoughtfulness of this video, and you make some good points about how little direct impact most news have on our daily lives. 

However, I would argue that in modern-day America, it would be unwise to completely disengage from any news. I would restrict to reading them only about 10-15min/day, just to stay informed. Otherwise you’re like an ostrich with his head stuck in the sand, but with a fire around him. You have to be informed enough to know when it’s time to leave. 

Remaining informed about your local government and country equips us to prevent tragedies from happening. I wish my German ancestors had been more informed about the news.
